title: Migrate pallet-conviction-voting to using fungible traits
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Migrate `pallet-conviction-voting` from the deprecated `Currency`/`LockableCurrency` traits to
    the `fungible` traits, replacing the `pyconvot` balance lock with a
    `FreezeReason::ConvictionVoting` freeze.

    Runtime changes required:
    - Replace `type Currency` with `type Fungible` and add
      `type RuntimeFreezeReason = RuntimeFreezeReason`.
    - Register `pallet_conviction_voting::migrations::v1::LazyMigrationV0ToV1<Runtime, (), Balances>`
      (once per instance) in `pallet_migrations::Config::Migrations`.

    The multi-block migration walks `ClassLocksFor` and, for each account, sets a freeze equal to
    the largest class lock and only then removes the old lock, so the voting balance stays
    restricted throughout. If the freeze cannot be set for an account, its old lock is kept, an
    error is logged and the migration continues with the next account. The on-chain storage
    version is set to 1 when the migration completes.

    The old lock used `WithdrawReasons::except(RESERVE)`. In `pallet-balances`, locks and freezes
    feed the same `frozen` amount, which `free + reserved` may not drop below, so the effective
    restriction is unchanged: the funds still cannot be transferred or used to pay fees, and can
    still be placed on hold.
crates:
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: major
- name: kitchensink-runtime
  bump: major
- name: pallet-staking-async-parachain-runtime
  bump: major
- name: pallet-staking-async-rc-runtime
  bump: major
- name: pallet-conviction-voting
  bump: major
